# Side Sheet / Modal Overlay Z-Index

Side sheets, drawer overlays, and full-screen modal backdrops must **always** render on top of the sticky navigation bar and all page content.

## Z-Index Ladder

| Layer | z-index | Purpose |
|-------|---------|---------|
| Skip link | 10000 | Accessibility — first focusable element |
| Nav (.nav) | 10001 | Sticky top navigation |
| Nav dropdowns | 10002 | Menus, user profile dropdown |
| **Modal overlay** | **10010** | Side sheets, drawers, modal backdrops |
| Modal content | 10011+ | Dialog content inside overlay |

## Rule

`.modal-overlay` (and any equivalent full-screen backdrop for side sheets or drawers) **must** use `z-index: 10010` — never `10000` or lower.

The drawer/modal content inside the overlay inherits correct stacking automatically; no separate `z-index` is needed on the drawer itself.

## Example

```css
.modal-overlay {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
    backdrop-filter: blur(4px);
    z-index: 10010;  /* Above nav (10001) and dropdowns (10002) */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
}
```

For side sheet layouts (e.g. `#hcModal`), use `align-items: flex-start; justify-content: flex-end;` — the z-index remains `10010`.
